{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Anna</b> — like <i>anna</i> in 'אנא חטא'; and it is an expression of thanks, for the word <b>annah</b> interchangeably has heh or alef, for two meanings: one time an expression of entreaty and one time an expression of thanks — like this instance, where he gives thanks to HaShem: <b>annah</b> YHWH, for I am Your servant — for this is not an expression of entreaty. But if one says <b>annah</b> YHWH, please save — it is an expression of entreaty. And so the word אולי: one time 'perhaps,' and one time like 'desiring' — אולי אוכל להלחם, אולי יהיה זה; and one time 'perhaps,' אולי לא תאבה האשה — from the mouth of the sage." "<b>You have loosened my bonds</b> — as if he were bound in chains, and the lamed is superfluous, like the lamed in <b>הרגו לאבנר</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {0 "The phrase מפי החכם at the end is unclear in context; rendered hyper-literally. The quoted phrases appear to be illustrative biblical idioms but are left unglossed by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:55.714106023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}